  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>We have&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>tan</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math><gwmw style=\"display:none;\"></gwmw></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>tan</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>tan</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>The graph of the two functions is given as</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/dc9c8849-d705-4da6-a308-ee6bf8a16e7e-image.png\" style=\"width: 393px; height: 340px;\" /></p><p>It is clear from the graph&nbsp;that the number of solutions of the given equation is<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p>",
